{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1443 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0a19413c2bc8e42354d0cb4672543bb630f0ea0d70ae4af586570c630dfcd6b2" :edb/db-before-t 1442 :edb/db-after-t 1443 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534755 50 #inst "2026-10-12T10:52:11.500Z" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186092025 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](images/22/220e8838850356768215ed74aefc469edbdc99aa50b9116729329f0e818d6978.svg)" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186092025 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](images/ad/add80202102548e61880979bc0379e0bc65f9ef7fa37173f9035410661e2b75e.png)" 13194139534755 17592186045417 false] [17592186092026 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+x+z=0 \\\\ z+4y-5=2 \\\\ 1+2x-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186092026 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3y+x+z=0 \\\\ z+4y-5=2 \\\\ 1+2x-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534755 17592186045417 false] [17592186092026 1074 "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](images/e8/e816a0fcde823bc6f6e88dff0a02c1877275cbed75757c1eb366fb224629127e.svg)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/be/beb80ea3185fc723c294313b63274554ec8af3531ed5643173a6127c59a21bb3.svg)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/e6/e6fac5dd0a9918a03ce7c14e9cd05a06c6d11e95346f261ec75d6ebea09de1d6.svg)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](images/72/72b9d627d372d7a64a271b555b0d4cbb89b2bf9d602cdec64b1d8987a5e21521.svg)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186092026 1074 "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](images/97/97d3c148b792d9db50bc81b8c12f1574f284746cb37b12d99a8881853bf5ea13.png)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/e9/e93ae11a2b2d1538c4ad97bba6d92e8e17fe14c8778898365ffeda9c5d1bacee.png)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/c2/c2492650916d7a880ea52322edb41b8127b4c31bcff0620cec3cf4e37fa7928f.png)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](images/dd/dd70742ae3c6613f78305edc718b10568269b49be611643059a1e6121828f404.png)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" 13194139534755 17592186045417 false] [17592186092185 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435149 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186092186 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435147 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186092187 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435148 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186092406 1050 960.0 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186237810 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z=6 \\\\ 4x+7y+2z=0 \\\\ 3x+y+z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186237810 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z=6 \\\\ 4x+7y+2z=0 \\\\ 3x+y+z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534755 17592186045417 false] [17592186435129 1080 "3" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186435129 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186435129 1083 #uuid "039d5f33-dfa0-51c2-93be-2b7000137d8a" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186435130 1080 "2" 13194139534755 17592186045417 true] [17592186435130 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 1319